title AMUS8 — Constel census: announce, collect, and know who is present
prompt Keaton set the recursion loop on the 1024-round itinerary and six-season double-seat: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, make progress before checking in, send often as its own signed round, stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Third lap of the turn. AMUS7 (gossip/broadcast) landed and sent — one voice reaches the whole sky at once. But an announce is only half a round. Lindy-first crux-first: every real protocol needs the OTHER half — collect the replies and know who answered. A heartbeat, a roll call, a quorum vote all share one shape (announce · reply · tally), and the constel consensus track already sketched (pond/apps/constel_consensus*.rye) needs exactly this tally. So AMUS8 closes the round the socket-gated ladder can still build purely.
think The one genuinely new concern: collect-and-tally. announce broadcasts the caller's greeting (the ping); respond has a member drain the ping it heard (proving reachability — an un-announced member has nothing to drain and refuses NeedMoreBytes) and reply its OWN greeting as a present token (no new frame kind — a member's greeting IS "I am here"); hear reads one reply off the caller's mailbox at the naming-law border and returns the responder's roster slot; take_census interleaves respond+hear so the caller's inbox holds one reply at a time. The tally is a fixed [max_piers]bool by slot — a silent member is a slot left false, so absence is knowable BY SLOT, not merely a smaller count.
think Bound reasoning that shaped the design: the caller's mailbox (channel max 2*max_frame=252 bytes) cannot hold seven ~64-byte replies at once (448 > 252), so a naive collect-all-then-read would ChannelFull for a full constellation. Interleaving respond+hear keeps the inbox to one reply at a time and makes the round bounded for any size up to max_piers — proven by block 6 (a census of eight completes clean). Gave the double-count its own honest error (CensusError.DoubleCount) rather than overloading NoSuchPier.
obs Witness GREEN on the first run. Six proofs: a full census in a sky of four sees exactly the three others present (the caller never itself); a silent member is detected by SLOT (count two, slot 2 false); a reply proves the ear (an un-announced member refuses NeedMoreBytes); a vowel-bearing reply refuses VowelPresent at the caller's border; a stranger cannot open a census (NoSuchPier before any announce); and a full constellation of eight censuses without ChannelFull. Witness GREEN, TAME bans clean, width exit 0; prior AMUS rungs stay GREEN (additive).
obs Kept docs synced (docs-implementation-sync): constel/README.md gains the census rung, the run block lists amus_census_witness, Status and Kin weave include AMUS8, the road-on names the census closing the gossip round, and the stamp advanced to 051525. The socket remains the only rung that stops for Keaton's word.
loom witness=amus_census_witness blocks=6 constellation_piers=4 present_counted=3 full_constellation=8 max_channel_bytes=252 greeting_frame_bytes=64 wall_ms_note=selftest under a second after build
file active-designing/20260814-051119_amus8-constel-census-liveness-round.md the AMUS8 design — announce/respond/hear/take_census, the tally by slot, the six proofs
file constel/census.rye AMUS8 — the collect half of a gossip round: interleaved respond+hear tallying who is present, a silent member known by slot
file tools/amus_census_witness.rish the GREEN witness for AMUS8
file constel/README.md kept synced — the census rung, run block, Status, Kin, road-on, and stamp
recommend check-in (Claude) — three AMUS rungs landed and sent this turn (switchboard · gossip · census); the pure-local Constel stack now stands up a many-pier constellation, routes point-to-point, broadcasts one-to-many, and closes a full liveness round with a present/silent tally. The next AMUS rung is either the socket (a custody gate — real transport, seed/comlink/, stops for Keaton's word) or a genuine consensus/quorum primitive over the census (a larger design worth a fresh read and, arguably, a seam check-in since it approaches the Mycelium consensus the six-season doc names improving on TigerBeetle/Mysticeti). Plenty of other agent-doable double-seat work remains too (Season A/D/F journeys), so this is a natural check-in on where to point the next arc, not a gates-only stop. Clock note: America/New_York read 20260814.051525, earlier than the prior newest 081900; the one-clock monotonic law honored by stamping 082400, just after the work it follows.
